        "original_id": "7ad914ba-47a9-55aa-b9d2-a768525b5809",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franklin Pierce, Lewis Cass, James Buchanan, Stephen A. Douglas, Andrew Jackson, Duncan McArthur\n- Events: 1852 Democratic National Convention, Treaty of Fort Meigs\n- Organizations: United States Senate, United States Cabinet\n- Places: Michigan, Pennsylvania, Illinois, Detroit\n- Groups: Wyandot, Seneca, Delaware, Shawnee, Potawatomi, Ottawa, Chippewa\n- Music: Search the City\n\nFacts:\n- The Treaty of Fort Meigs was signed on September 29, 1817 between the United States and chiefs and warriors of the Wyandot, Seneca, Delaware, Shawnee, Potawatomi, Ottawa, and Chippewa, with Lewis Cass and Duncan McArthur representing the United States.\n- Lewis Cass was born on October 9, 1782, and died on June 17, 1866.\n- Lewis Cass was an American military officer, politician, and statesman.\n- Lewis Cass represented Michigan in the United States Senate.\n- Lewis Cass served in the Cabinets of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.\n- Lewis Cass was the Democratic presidential nominee in 1848.\n- The 1852 Democratic National Convention nominated Franklin Pierce for President on the 49th ballot as a dark horse candidate.\n- The 1852 Democratic National Convention passed over Lewis Cass of Michigan, James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois.\n- Search the City was an alternative and punk band from Detroit, Michigan.\n- Search the City released two EPs and two studio albums.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "da67cbae-762b-55da-aba5-cb2b2df9504f",
        "text": "Page: 1852 Democratic National Convention. Sentence: The 1852 Democratic National Convention nominated the dark horse candidate Franklin Pierce for President on the 49th ballot, passing over better known candidates Lewis Cass of Michigan (the previous nominee in 1848), James Buchanan of Pennsylvania, and Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois.\nPage: Lewis Cass. Sentence: Lewis Cass (October 9, 1782June 17, 1866) was an American military officer, politician, and statesman.\nPage: Lewis Cass. Sentence: He represented Michigan in the United States Senate and served in the Cabinet of Andrew Jackson and James Buchanan.\nPage: Treaty of Fort Meigs. Sentence: The Treaty of Fort Meigs, also called the Treaty of the Foot of the Rapids, was signed September 29, 1817 between the chiefs and warriors of the Wyandot, Seneca, Delaware, Shawnee, Potawatomi, Ottawa and Chippewa, tribes of Native Americans and the United States of America, represented by Lewis Cass and Duncan McArthur.\nPage: Search the City. Sentence: Search the City was an alternative and punk band from Detroit, Michigan who released two EPs and two studio albums.",
